Some users see another user's recommendations. User 1 viewing item 23 sometimes gets the result computed for user 12 viewing item 3. The recommendation model is deterministic and has been verified separately.

```python
_cache = {}

def cache_key(user_id, item_id):
    return f"{user_id}{item_id}"

def compute_recommendation(user_id, item_id):
    return f"recs-for-user-{user_id}-item-{item_id}"

def get_recommendation(user_id, item_id):
    key = cache_key(user_id, item_id)
    if key not in _cache:
        _cache[key] = compute_recommendation(user_id, item_id)
    return _cache[key]

get_recommendation(12, 3)
print(get_recommendation(1, 23))  # recs-for-user-12-item-3
```

